.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- extract zip archives with colon-path member mapping
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I zipfile
.RI [ member ]...
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path aware wrapper around
.BR unzip (1).
By default (when
.B COLON_WRAP
is unset), a built-in rewrite implementation extracts colon-path members
to their
.I LEAF
paths on disk.
Set
.B COLON_WRAP=1
to invoke
.B unzip
from
.B PATH
instead.
.PP
When a member is given as
.BR BASE:LEAF ,
archive members under the physical path
.B BASE/LEAF
are extracted and written to
.I LEAF
on disk.
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ a.zip a/b:/c/d/e
Extracts members
.B a/b/c/d/e/**
from
.B a.zip
and writes them to
.BR c/d/e/** .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Describe the extract/relocate plan without executing it.
When using the built-in rewrite (default), output is prefixed with
.BR (rewrite) .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List archive contents.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Test archive integrity.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose list or test.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-archive\-comment
Show archive comment only.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-extract\-to\-stdout
Extract files to stdout.
.TP
.B \-c
Extract to stdout (alias).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Freshen existing files only.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Update only if archive member is newer.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-never\-overwrite
Never overwrite existing files.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-overwrite
Overwrite existing files without prompting.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-junk\-paths
Junk directory paths when extracting.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-directory=DIR
Extract files into
.IR DIR .
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude=GLOB
Exclude files matching
.IR GLOB .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode.
.TP
.B \-qq
Very quiet mode.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-password=PASS
Decrypt encrypted entries.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-charset=CHARSET
Charset for zip entry names.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-output\-dir=DIR
Output directory for extracted files.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-workdir=DIR
Use
.I DIR
as temporary work directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLON_WRAP
When unset (default), use the built-in rewrite implementation.
When set to
.BR 1 ,
exec the stem of
.B $0
from
.B PATH
(\fBcolon-unzip\fR → \fBunzip\fR).
When set to a program name, exec that program instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unzip (1),
.BR colon-zip (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
